    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm not sure I'm comfortable saying the results are \"generalizable\" with only 12 people. That feels like an invitation for a reviewer to reject us immediately for overreaching. If we can't claim generalizability, how do we actually defend the strength of the data without making it look like we just didn't have the budget for a real study?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
